{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146807-how-to-make-use-of-cumbersome-tools-or-i-m-chargin-mah-laser","id":1146807,"title":"How to make use of cumbersome Tools, or \"I'm chargin mah laser!\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-04T14:44:37-07:00","id":1146807,"title":"How to make use of cumbersome Tools, or \"I'm chargin mah laser!\"","content":"So, I've been considering for a while now something that was never quite clear to me, that many foci/tools/instruments listed don't seem particularly useful for a typical adventuring party. Mage has a nasty history of people trying to powergame and minmax their way into more convenient and powerful fast-casting, which both on its face discourages the creation of characters who use interesting but awkward tools, as well as leads to less creative roleplay. I've always considered the requirement to <i>really</i> roleplay to be one of the biggest strengths of Mage, so this has been a bit of a conundrum for me.<br /> <br /> Is it possible/allowable/rules legal to effectively &quot;charge up&quot; spell power to be expended later, in order to make use of cumbersome instruments and enable otherwise less-contributing Paradigms? For example, there is an Ecstatic or Verbena character who uses sex as a tool. Naturally sex can't be used in the heat of battle to do something, and is equally hard to use &quot;in the field&quot; even outside of combat. Of course, this tool may be better suited for rituals, but perhaps it could be used to charge up &quot;sexual energy,&quot; so long as the &quot;charging&quot; process is done in a in-Paradigm manner, like hunting for a vampire. Maybe that sexual energy is enough to cast one Effect at a later time. This is probably one of the more free form kinds of &quot;charging up&quot; that I've thought of.<br /> <br /> Other examples could include &quot;brewing up potions&quot; or &quot;preparing spells on written, disposable paper that burns when used to cast the spell.&quot; Perhaps these mages could roll Crafts or Esoterica to generate the number of &quot;charges.&quot; In these cases, the mage would specify what the desired Effect for each &quot;charge&quot; is to prevent over-preparing, and each spell is consumed upon casting.<br /> <br /> In all of these cases, the final Arete roll would always be done at the time of casting, and a failed roll consumes the &quot;charge.&quot; However, there wouldn't be any &quot;fast-casting&quot; penalties against these mages if using the charge.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T16:21:34-07:00","id":1146835,"title":"","content":"I let people who have &quot;life style&quot; type Tools have a &quot;fast use&quot; version. Some one who has &quot;Sex&quot; or &quot;Strict Abstainence&quot; as their Tool does something to get in touch with their primal casting they did earlier to cast the effect in game. A potion brewer might spend much of their down time working on potions but they &quot;just need a couple seconds to make it work&quot;<br /> <br /> But then for example I consider most tools requiring alot of lifestyle work, someone who has Martial arts as their Tool has to spend alot of time training for example. The Hermetic who has sigils as thing spends hours on end working them out. The &quot;cheap fast&quot; stuff is the benefits of being good with your tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T19:39:46-07:00","id":1146886,"title":"","content":"For how the things work that'd depend on paradigm. For example a Potion you could easily roll Ar\u00eate as and Extended casting and you devote some successess to duration providing a shelf life for the potion (or indeed the Rote may detail this in specific). Also, when it comes to the &quot;Cumbersome Tools&quot; dont forget that many of them are Rotes as well as Foci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T02:16:26-07:00","id":1146945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146807-how-to-make-use-of-cumbersome-tools-or-i-m-chargin-mah-laser?p=1146835#post1146835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I let people who have &quot;life style&quot; type Tools have a &quot;fast use&quot; version. Some one who has &quot;Sex&quot; or &quot;Strict Abstainence&quot; as their Tool does something to get in touch with their primal casting they did earlier to cast the effect in game. A potion brewer might spend much of their down time working on potions but they &quot;just need a couple seconds to make it work&quot;<br /> <br /> But then for example I consider most tools requiring alot of lifestyle work, someone who has Martial arts as their Tool has to spend alot of time training for example. The Hermetic who has sigils as thing spends hours on end working them out. The &quot;cheap fast&quot; stuff is the benefits of being good with your tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this was the specific reasoning given in the Revised Order of Hermes book. When asked how fair it was that Hermetics had to perform lengthy and complicated rituals, the book pointed out that it was no more time consuming as the hours Akashics spend meditating and practicing kata, or the hours and materials an Etherite spent building their death ray. Mages arguably always use Lifestyle-As-Magick, since Magick is itself a Lifestyle.<br /> <br /> Further, most of those lifestyle works are built around preparing the Mage to have the tools and techniques they need for faster magick. If a Hermetic can't draw a magic circle on the ground and chant for an hour, they use a wand (usually a wand that was prepared and consecrated and imbued with power through another, earlier hours-long bout of crafting and chanting).<br /> <br /> However, those tools could be ruled as being specifically created for specific magical tasks. If you want to encourage more involved spellcasting, you could make it so that quick or convenient magick works for Rotes, but less well for crafting more freeform spells. That wand might be useful for telekinetically moving around large objects or making the user float, but may not be up to the challenge of moving the tumblers in a lock to unlock a door. The wand wasn't specifically designed to do that. Some Hermetics may even have Paradigms that require them to develop many different wands for different elements or areas to manipulate, because fire has different correspondences, invokes different figures of the godhead, and needs a wand made from a different kind of wood than lightning or levitation. If they incorporate Celestial Alignments into their style, the astrological signs and position of planets could also factor into what spells they can quickly cast. Casting offensive magick could be rendered more difficult if Mars - the planet of war - is in retrograde, whereas a teleportation spell might be easy if Mercury is strong at the time.<br /> <br /> In such cases, the Hermetic might need to perform more involved spells, since they're having to work without the right tool for the job, or having to work around the inappropriate star alignment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T08:01:40-07:00","id":1147041,"title":"","content":"I suppose I wasn't completely clear about the &quot;charging up&quot; component of the question. Just to be clear, I mean that there are no Arete rolls during the &quot;prep&quot; phase, such as the ritual sex, or the potion making, or the scroll writing. Additionally, all of this &quot;prep&quot; is completely non-magickal until the moment that the spell is cast. Potions do nothing, scrolls do nothing, until that last moment when the mage invokes those tools. They all simply serve to satisfy the mage's beliefs and will.<br /> <br /> Of course, the filling up of the sexual energy tank is something else entirely. Perhaps it could be tied to one Sphere, or still even tighter down to one specific Effect that's thematic to the act? The Life Sphere, or a specific healing/boost spell. Again, Arete wouldn't be rolled until the mage wants to actually use the &quot;energy,&quot; and there could be no retroactive &quot;yeah, I went and did my sex thing a bunch last night, so I can just cast freely.&quot; One spell, or maybe more depending on a supporting roll during the &quot;charging up&quot; prep during the previous evening. Similar preparation could be done by, say, an Akashic charging up their chi for one big strike, to be determined later, but once it's gone, it has to be recharged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T08:22:50-07:00","id":1147048,"title":"","content":"Well here's how I do it. Rather than having a bunch of free castings from stuff like say &quot;Ritual purity&quot; the character maintains ritual purity generally(no touching the unclean, no eating the wrong foods, no sex) but when they want to cast magick they spend a turn doing something to get them in touch with their practice like someone who chants or draws a sigil or what have you.<br /> <br /> Similarly I wouldn't have someone who's Tool is sex have to say masturbate everytime they want to cast something simple but that they probably do need it for extended rituals AND when they need something on a smaller more regular fashion they do something to symbolically get in touch with the last time they had sex.<br /> <br /> I have a similar situation for people who want try psionics as their practice. <br /> <br /> Unless someone takes unique or specialized Tools I try to give everyone the same chance and assume they are doing a bunch of lifestyle stuff because as Bluecho said, &quot;Magic is a lifestyle&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T08:43:20-07:00","id":1147060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I wasn't completely clear about the &quot;charging up&quot; component of the question. Just to be clear, I mean that there are no Arete rolls during the &quot;prep&quot; phase, such as the ritual sex, or the potion making, or the scroll writing. Additionally, all of this &quot;prep&quot; is completely non-magickal until the moment that the spell is cast. Potions do nothing, scrolls do nothing, until that last moment when the mage invokes those tools. They all simply serve to satisfy the mage's beliefs and will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. This is what Bluecho said, note how the post never mentions Arete rolls. It's pure fluff. It's what makes sense to the player. You don't need to prepate a potion so it will work like a Charm, you just have various potions or gadgets that do general stuff.<br /> <br /> For instance, I have an Etherite that uses a camera to do magic, this is a special camera created to perceive stuff, and so I use it mostly to perceive stuff. The camera it's useless to people that isn't me because &quot;they don't understand how it works&quot;. Also, I could &quot;McGuiver&quot; it in a turn or two to make it shot a laser if I really needed (albeit this would involve making the camera unable to perceive stuff until I undo the changes, and I can't do this if I'm evading bullets or something like that). I even used the flash of the camera to magically blind an enemy one time, when I hadn't time to do any modifications, because it's an instrument and I know how to take advantage of all it's capabilities.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, you can load yourself of sexual energy or pray at your monolith to get the favor of the gods. Just don't overdo it, It should be good to justify one type of magic. You could use the ritual as a &quot;gadget&quot; of sorts: For instance, you pray at your monolith so the gods provide you with &quot;the power over fire&quot;, and so now you have it (pyrokinesis). Perhaps your &quot;vow of poverty&quot; provides you with god luck (god luck entropy magick). You should work with the ST to determine how many &quot;powers&quot; you can have at a time, and how dynamic they can be. You probably can't &quot;McGuiver&quot; a Vow (you're supposed to obey it), but it's benefits may be intangible enough to justify various effects<br /> <br /> In the case of &quot;filling your tank&quot; with energy or having potions, you may have &quot;charges&quot;, like a D&amp;D sorcerer, that has a number of castings before exhausting the &quot;tank&quot;. Probably potions have specific uses (being more like a D&amp;D mage that has to memorize spells), but it's also true that you may be able to &quot;McGuiver&quot; with them (I.E, combining two potions to create an effect you didn't know you needed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-05-2017, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}